<!-- Commands.md, table of commands: rows (the boss commands are shared by Ultron, Thanos and Apocalypse; whoever stitches keeps one copy) -->
| `/enhanced boss start apocalypse [force]` | Wakes En Sabah Nur at your feet, with no Capstone. `force` skips the checks of the ground, the sky and the need for a Scarlet Witch or a Phoenix (not Peaceful, not the switch that turns him off, not the one-fight-at-a-time rule). See [Apocalypse](Apocalypse). |
| `/enhanced boss stop` | Ends the running boss fight (the Capstone is given back, if one was used). |
| `/enhanced boss list` | Lists the running boss fights. |

<!-- Commands.md, table "Powers": one row -->
| `apocalypse` | [Apocalypse](Apocalypse) |

<!-- Commands.md, table "Looks": one row -->
| Apocalypse | `apocalypse`, `en_sabah_nur`, `own` |

<!-- Commands.md, table "Examples": rows -->
| `/enhanced boss start apocalypse force` | Wakes En Sabah Nur where you stand, with no Capstone and no one to break his shield. |
| `/enhanced power set Steve apocalypse en_sabah_nur` | Makes Steve Apocalypse, in the 3600 BC look (he skips the boss and the Essence). |

<!-- Commands.md, section "Looking at the animations": a line under /enhanced_anim, or a short section of its own -->
`/enhanced_model apocalypse <state>` is a game-only command for the people who draw: it shows a copy of En Sabah Nur in a state (`idle`, `awakening`, `tell_lance`, `tell_wave`, `tell_spikes`, `tell_boulders`, `tell_entomb`, `tell_mind_crush`, `tell_portal`, `backhand`, `tell_tornado`, `staggered`, `hover`, `escaping`, `kneeling`, `armour_fall`, `dying`, `withdrawing`, `true_<state>` for the frail body, `dying_fire`, the shield's states `shield_up`, `shield_cracked`, `shield_forming`, `shield_reforming` and `shield_broken`; `sand_cocoon`, `sand_lance` and `sand_boulder` have a command of their own), frozen at a tick. `/enhanced_model list` shows what can be shown.
